{"name":"More Than a Week","hex":"#8d8d8d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"more","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["comparative degree of many: in greater number.","comparative degree of much: in greater quantity, amount, or proportion."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To a greater degree or extent. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Used to form the comparative form of adjectives and adverbs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/more"},{"term":"than","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["Used in comparisons, to introduce the basis of comparison.","Because; for."]},{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Introduces a comparison, and is associated with comparatives, and with words such as more, less, and fewer. Typically, it seeks to measure the force of an adjective or similar description between two predicates."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/than"},{"term":"week","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any period of seven consecutive days.","A period of seven days beginning with Sunday or Monday."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["The squeal of a pig."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/week"}],"entries":[{"title":"More Than","blocks":[{"text":"More Than is an insurance company based in the United Kingdom. Having previously provided car, home and travel insurance before exiting those markets in 2024, More Than currently only offers pet insurance. Its business arm More Than BUSINESS offered business insurance. The company is a subsidiary of the RSA Insurance Group."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/More_Than","wikidata":"Q20713193"},{"title":"Than","blocks":[{"text":"Than is a grammatical particle analyzed as both a conjunction and a preposition in the English language. It introduces a comparison and is associated with comparatives and with words such as more, less, and fewer. Typically, it measures the force of an adjective or similar description between two predicates."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Than","wikidata":"Q7710078"},{"title":"Week","blocks":[{"text":"A week is a unit of time equal to seven days. It is the standard calendrical period between a day and a month in most parts of the world. There are just over 52 weeks in a year, or on average 4+1⁄3 weeks in a month. The days of the week are often used to set work days, rest days, and holy days. The term \"week\" is also used to refer to a sub-section of the week, such as the workweek and weekend. Certain weeks within a year may be designated for a particular purpose, such as Golden Week in China and Japan. More informally, certain groups may advocate awareness weeks, such as National Family Week in Canada, which are designed to draw attention to a certain subject or cause."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/First_Day_of_Week_World_Map.svg/330px-First_Day_of_Week_World_Map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Week","wikidata":"Q23387"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Italian_-_Bracelet_-_Walters_41269.jpg/500px-Italian_-_Bracelet_-_Walters_41269.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Italian_-_Bracelet_-_Walters_41269.jpg/1280px-Italian_-_Bracelet_-_Walters_41269.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Italian_-_Bracelet_-_Walters_41269.jpg/500px-Italian_-_Bracelet_-_Walters_41269.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Italian cameo bracelet representing the days of the week by their eponymous deities (mid-19th century, Walters Art Museum)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalian_-_Bracelet_-_Walters_41269.jpg"},{